# ML5-E nightly retraining cron — operator reference
# =====================================================
#
# This is a REFERENCE for the operator's `crontab -e`. The extension NEVER
# installs or writes a crontab. Copy the relevant lines into your crontab.
#
# The cron runs at 2:00 AM local time every night. It:
#   1. Re-exports the corpus snapshot (new redacted-tagged sessions).
#   2. If no new rows since the last run → exits 0 (no-op, no training noise).
#   3. Otherwise calls ML5-A train → ML5-B bench → ML5-C package.
#   4. Appends a PromotionV1 ledger row to the append-only manifest.
#   5. Runs the promotion gate: all five heads must pass per-head calibration
#      thresholds AND the new asset must beat the committed asset on a fixed
#      held-out dev set. On fail → candidate recorded as demoted_new_asset.
#   6. Candidates land in ~/.pi/mega-compact-encoder/candidates/. The human
#      operator reviews the dashboard and promotes via the ML5-D "Improve
#      Cortex" flow — the cron NEVER commits or pushes.
#
# Environment:
#   MEGACOMPACT_ML5_E=1         Enable the ML5-E nightly retraining loop.
#   MEGACOMPACT_STATE_DIR       Path to the extension state dir (default:
#                               ~/.pi/agent/extensions/pi-mega-compact).
#
# All computation is local — zero network (PREVENT-PI-004).

# Nightly retraining at 2:00 AM local time.
0 2 * * * cd ~/pi-mega-compact && MEGACOMPACT_ML5_E=1 node scripts/ml5/retrain-nightly.mjs >> ~/.pi/mega-compact-encoder/retrain.log 2>&1
